One main important issue as well was the two VMs which are the kali Linux VM,the Wazuh Manager VM, and the main OS were not "reaching" each other.
To start up, I purposely set both VMs to "bridged adapter network" so that each VM can have its own IP address within the network which will make the project more
realistic (realizing each VM as a separate device). However, the main issue is that the connectivity test "ping" wasn't returning anything when done.
When pinging my windows main OS from my kali and wazuh manager, nothing returned. This turned out to be a firewall/security restriction in windows settings that was 
simply solved by allowing the ICMP protocol, which when i allowed, made the connectivity normal again and made all OSs reachable. 
